IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967, section 4 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- Nothing here has been checked against a decided case.

§ `Fixtures -- bodies`

GIVEN `kind` IS A BodyKind,
      `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declared by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `head office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cooperative society flag` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `LLP flag` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Body
DECIDE `a body` `kind` `in Singapore` `declared by the Minister` `head office in Singapore` `cooperative society flag` `LLP flag` IS
    Body WITH
        `what it is` IS `kind`
        `incorporated in Singapore` IS `in Singapore`
        `declared by the Minister in the Gazette a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or not incorporated for commercial purposes` IS `declared by the Minister`
        `has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore` IS `head office in Singapore`
        `a cooperative society` IS `cooperative society flag`
        `a limited liability partnership within section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS `LLP flag`

`a Singapore company` MEANS `a body` `a company incorporated under this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a Singapore statutory board declared by the Minister` MEANS `a body` `a body corporate formed in Singapore that is not a company` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a Singapore body corporate the Minister has not declared` MEANS `a body` `a body corporate formed in Singapore that is not a company` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a corporation sole` MEANS `a body` `a corporation sole` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a Singapore cooperative society` MEANS `a body` `a cooperative society` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a registered trade union` MEANS `a body` `a registered trade union` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a registered platform work association` MEANS `a body` `a platform work association` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a Singapore limited liability partnership` MEANS `a body` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a Delaware company` MEANS `a body` `a body incorporated outside Singapore` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a cooperative society incorporated abroad` MEANS `a body` `a body incorporated outside Singapore` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a limited liability partnership formed abroad` MEANS `a body` `a body incorporated outside Singapore` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a foreign public authority declared by the Minister` MEANS `a body` `a body incorporated outside Singapore` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary` MEANS `a body` `an unincorporated body with a foreign place of origin that may sue or be sued through its secretary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the same association, with its head office in Singapore` MEANS `a body` `an unincorporated body with a foreign place of origin that may sue or be sued through its secretary` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a bare partnership` MEANS `a body` `something that is not a body corporate and not a foreign body` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4(1) "corporation" and "foreign company"`

#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `a Singapore company`
#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `a Singapore body corporate the Minister has not declared`
#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `a Delaware company`

-- The six exclusions, (a), (b), (c), (d), (da) and (e).
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a Singapore statutory board declared by the Minister`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a corporation sole`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a Singapore cooperative society`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a registered trade union`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a registered platform work association`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a Singapore limited liability partnership`

-- Exclusion (a) is confined to bodies incorporated in Singapore. The same declaration
-- over a foreign body takes nothing out.
#ASSERT `the body falls within an exclusion from "corporation"` `a Singapore statutory board declared by the Minister`
#ASSERT NOT `the body falls within an exclusion from "corporation"` `a foreign public authority declared by the Minister`
#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `a foreign public authority declared by the Minister`

-- Exclusion (c) is unqualified as to where the society was formed, so a foreign
-- cooperative society is both a foreign company (limb (a) names a "society") and
-- excluded. The words "but does not include" let the exclusion prevail.
#ASSERT `the body is a foreign company` `a cooperative society incorporated abroad`
#ASSERT `the body falls within an exclusion from "corporation"` `a cooperative society incorporated abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a cooperative society incorporated abroad`

-- Exclusion (e) means a limited liability partnership under the Limited Liability
-- Partnerships Act 2005, so one formed abroad is not excluded.
#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `a limited liability partnership formed abroad`

-- "Foreign company" limb (b): an UNINCORPORATED body is a corporation for the whole Act.
#ASSERT `the body is a foreign company` `an unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is within the first limb of "corporation"` `an unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary`
#ASSERT `the body is a corporation` `an unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary`

-- With its head office in Singapore it falls out of limb (b).
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a foreign company` `the same association, with its head office in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `the same association, with its head office in Singapore`

#ASSERT NOT `the body is a corporation` `a bare partnership`
#ASSERT `the body is a foreign company` `a Delaware company`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a foreign company` `a Singapore company`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a foreign company` `a Singapore cooperative society`

§ `Fixtures -- company status`

GIVEN `incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `private before 1967` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `private by section 18` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `converted under section 31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ceased to be private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CompanyStatus
DECIDE `a status` `incorporated` `private before 1967` `private by section 18` `converted under section 31(1)` `ceased to be private` IS
    CompanyStatus WITH
        `incorporated under this Act or a corresponding previous written law` IS `incorporated`
        `was a private company immediately before 29 December 1967 under the repealed written laws` IS `private before 1967`
        `was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` IS `private by section 18`
        `was converted into a private company under section 31(1)` IS `converted under section 31(1)`
        `has since ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32` IS `ceased to be private`

`a company incorporated as private under section 18` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a company converted to private under section 31(1)` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a company that was private before 29 December 1967` MEANS `a status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a private company that has since ceased to be one` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a company with no route to private status` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`something that is not a company at all` MEANS `a status` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4(1) "company", "private company", "public company"`

#ASSERT `the company is a private company` `a company incorporated as private under section 18`
#ASSERT `the company is a private company` `a company converted to private under section 31(1)`
#ASSERT `the company is a private company` `a company that was private before 29 December 1967`
#ASSERT NOT `the company is a public company` `a company incorporated as private under section 18`

-- "Which has not ceased to be a private company": a company that has since ceased
-- is public, because a public company is simply one that is not private.
#ASSERT NOT `the company is a private company` `a private company that has since ceased to be one`
#ASSERT `the company is a public company` `a private company that has since ceased to be one`

-- A company that cannot be traced to limb (a), (b) or (c) is public by default.
#ASSERT `the company is a public company` `a company with no route to private status`

-- Something that is not a company is neither.
#ASSERT NOT `the company is a company` `something that is not a company at all`
#ASSERT NOT `the company is a private company` `something that is not a company at all`
#ASSERT NOT `the company is a public company` `something that is not a company at all`

§ `Fixtures -- exempt private companies`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body, `beneficial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Shareholder
DECIDE `a shareholder` `the body` `beneficial` IS
    Shareholder WITH
        `the body` IS `the body`
        `holds a beneficial interest in the shares directly or indirectly` IS `beneficial`

GIVEN `the status` IS A CompanyStatus,
      `the number of members` IS A NUMBER,
      `government owned and declared` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the holders` IS A LIST OF Shareholder
GIVETH A PrivateCompanyFacts
DECIDE `private company facts` `the status` `the number of members` `government owned and declared` `the holders` IS
    PrivateCompanyFacts WITH
        `the status` IS `the status`
        `the holders of beneficial interests` IS `the holders`
        `the number of members` IS `the number of members`
        `wholly owned by the Government and declared exempt by the Minister in the Gazette in the national interest` IS `government owned and declared`

`ten individuals` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 10 FALSE EMPTY
`exactly twenty individuals` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 20 FALSE EMPTY
`twenty-one individuals` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 21 FALSE EMPTY
`a public company with five members` MEANS `private company facts` `a company with no route to private status` 5 FALSE EMPTY

`held by a Singapore company` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore company` TRUE))
`held by a company that has only legal title` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore company` FALSE))
`held by a cooperative society` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore cooperative society` TRUE))
`held by a registered trade union` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a registered trade union` TRUE))
`held by a limited liability partnership` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore limited liability partnership` TRUE))
`held by a corporation sole` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a corporation sole` TRUE))
`held by a platform work association` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a registered platform work association` TRUE))
`held by a statutory board the Minister declared` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore statutory board declared by the Minister` TRUE))
`held by an unincorporated foreign association` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `an unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary` TRUE))
`held by a cooperative society formed abroad` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a cooperative society incorporated abroad` TRUE))
`held by a Delaware company` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 1 FALSE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Delaware company` TRUE))
`government owned, declared, many members, held by a company` MEANS `private company facts` `a company incorporated as private under section 18` 400 TRUE (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore company` TRUE))

§ `Section 4(1) "exempt private company"`

#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `ten individuals`

-- Not more than 20: twenty is in and twenty-one is out.
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `exactly twenty individuals`
#ASSERT NOT `the company is an exempt private company` `twenty-one individuals`

-- It has to be a private company at all.
#ASSERT NOT `the company is an exempt private company` `a public company with five members`

-- A beneficial interest held by a corporation defeats limb (a).
#ASSERT `some beneficial interest is held by a corporation` (LIST (`a shareholder` `a Singapore company` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a Singapore company`
#ASSERT NOT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a Delaware company`

-- But only a BENEFICIAL interest does.
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a company that has only legal title`

-- THE TWIST. "Corporation" has six exclusions, and a private company held by any of
-- them still qualifies. Six different kinds of owner, one result.
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a cooperative society`
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a registered trade union`
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a corporation sole`
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a platform work association`
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a statutory board the Minister declared`

-- A foreign cooperative society is excluded from "corporation", so it too is allowed.
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by a cooperative society formed abroad`

-- An unincorporated foreign association that can sue through its secretary is a
-- "foreign company" and so a "corporation", and defeats the exemption.
#ASSERT NOT `the company is an exempt private company` `held by an unincorporated foreign association`

-- Limb (b): wholly Government-owned and declared, with no ceiling on members and no
-- bar on corporate ownership.
#ASSERT `the company is an exempt private company` `government owned, declared, many members, held by a company`

§ `Fixtures -- directors and officers`

GIVEN `occupies the position` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `alternate or substitute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `directors accustomed to act on directions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that is by reason only of professional advice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PersonInRelationToBoard
DECIDE `a person` `occupies the position` `alternate or substitute` `directors accustomed to act on directions` `that is by reason only of professional advice` IS
    PersonInRelationToBoard WITH
        `occupies the position of director by whatever name called` IS `occupies the position`
        `is an alternate or substitute director` IS `alternate or substitute`
        `the directors or a majority of them are accustomed to act on this person's directions or instructions` IS `directors accustomed to act on directions`
        `that is by reason only that they act on this person's advice given in a professional capacity` IS `that is by reason only of professional advice`

`a named director` MEANS `a person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an alternate director` MEANS `a person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a shadow director` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a professional adviser whose advice is always followed` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`an adviser who is also directing in practice beyond advice` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a director who also happens to advise professionally` MEANS `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a stranger to the board` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4(1) "director" and 4(2), 4(10), 4(11)`

#ASSERT `the person is a director` `a named director`
#ASSERT `the person is a director` `an alternate director`
#ASSERT `the person is a director` `a shadow director`

-- s 4(2): the professional adviser is out, but only "by reason only" of the advice.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a director` `a professional adviser whose advice is always followed`
#ASSERT `the person is a director` `an adviser who is also directing in practice beyond advice`

-- A person who occupies the position is a director whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `the person is a director` `a director who also happens to advise professionally`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a director` `a stranger to the board`

-- s 4(10) and (11): with one director, "2 or more directors" is that director.
#ASSERT `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` 1 1
#ASSERT `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` 3 2
#ASSERT `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` 2 2
#ASSERT NOT `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` 3 1
#ASSERT NOT `a requirement that 2 or more directors act is met` 2 1

-- s 4(1) "officer": the inclusions and the exclusions.
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a director`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `the secretary`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a person employed in an executive capacity`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a receiver and manager appointed under a power in an instrument`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a liquidator in a voluntary winding up`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a receiver who is not also a manager`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a receiver and manager appointed by the Court`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a liquidator appointed by the Court`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a liquidator appointed by the creditors`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a judicial manager under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `some other office or none`

-- The same receiver and manager is an officer if appointed under an instrument and not
-- if appointed by the Court. Likewise the voluntary liquidator and the creditors' one.
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a receiver and manager appointed under a power in an instrument`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation` `a receiver and manager appointed by the Court`

§ `Section 4(1) "voting share"`

GIVEN `issued` IS A BOOLEAN, `any right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN, `votes in other circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ShareVotingRights
DECIDE `a share` `issued` `any right to vote` `votes in other circumstances` IS
    ShareVotingRights WITH
        `is an issued share` IS `issued`
        `has any right to vote attached in any circumstances` IS `any right to vote`
        `has a right to vote in some circumstance other than the six listed` IS `votes in other circumstances`

`an ordinary share` MEANS `a share` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a preference share that votes only on its own rights, a reduction, a winding up or while in arrear` MEANS `a share` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a share with no vote in any circumstances` MEANS `a share` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a share not yet issued` MEANS `a share` FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a preference share that also votes on appointing directors` MEANS `a share` TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the share is a voting share` `an ordinary share`
#ASSERT `the share is a voting share` `a preference share that also votes on appointing directors`
#ASSERT NOT `the share is a voting share` `a preference share that votes only on its own rights, a reduction, a winding up or while in arrear`
#ASSERT NOT `the share is a voting share` `a share with no vote in any circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `the share is a voting share` `a share not yet issued`

§ `Fixtures -- instruments`

GIVEN `a security` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a cheque or bill` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a promissory note` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `face value` IS A NUMBER,
      `maturity in months` IS A NUMBER,
      `prescribed exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `evidences deposit or loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Instrument
DECIDE `an instrument` `a security` `a cheque or bill` `a promissory note` `face value` `maturity in months` `prescribed exclusion` `evidences deposit or loan` IS
    Instrument WITH
        `is debenture stock, a bond, a note or another security of a corporation` IS `a security`
        `is a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange` IS `a cheque or bill`
        `is a promissory note` IS `a promissory note`
        `face value in dollars` IS `face value`
        `maturity in months` IS `maturity in months`
        `is a prescribed document excluded for this provision` IS `prescribed exclusion`
        `evidences indebtedness for money deposited or lent in response to an invitation to the public` IS `evidences deposit or loan`

`a bond` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE
`a cheque` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE
`a promissory note for exactly $100,000 over 12 months` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE 100000 12 FALSE FALSE
`a promissory note for $99,999 over 12 months` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE 99999 12 FALSE FALSE
`a promissory note for $100,000 over 13 months` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE 100000 13 FALSE FALSE
`a promissory note for $5,000,000 over 3 months` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5000000 3 FALSE FALSE
`a prescribed document excluded by regulation` MEANS `an instrument` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE
`a receipt for money lent to a company in response to a public invitation` MEANS `an instrument` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE
`a loan agreement between two companies` MEANS `an instrument` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4(1) "debenture", and 4(5)`

#ASSERT `the instrument is a debenture` `a bond`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument is a debenture` `a cheque`

-- The promissory-note carve-out needs BOTH a face value of at least $100,000 AND a
-- maturity of no more than 12 months.
#ASSERT `the promissory note falls within the section 4(1) carve-out` `a promissory note for exactly $100,000 over 12 months`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument is a debenture` `a promissory note for exactly $100,000 over 12 months`
#ASSERT `the instrument is a debenture` `a promissory note for $99,999 over 12 months`
#ASSERT `the instrument is a debenture` `a promissory note for $100,000 over 13 months`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument is a debenture` `a promissory note for $5,000,000 over 3 months`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument is a debenture` `a prescribed document excluded by regulation`

-- s 4(5A): a document acknowledging indebtedness for money lent in response to an
-- invitation to the public is deemed a debenture even though it is not otherwise a
-- security.
#ASSERT `the instrument is a debenture` `a receipt for money lent to a company in response to a public invitation`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument is a debenture` `a loan agreement between two companies`

-- s 4(5): the invitation itself.
#ASSERT `the invitation is deemed an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the invitation is deemed an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the invitation is deemed an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures` FALSE FALSE

§ `Sections 4(1) "listed", 4(13), 4(3), 4(4)`

#ASSERT `the corporation is listed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the corporation is listed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the corporation is listed` FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the memorandum and articles in force on 2 January 2016 are the company's constitution` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the memorandum and articles in force on 2 January 2016 are the company's constitution` FALSE
#ASSERT `a contract that refers to the articles of association now refers to the constitution`

-- s 4(3): untruth is about being misleading in context, not about literal falsity.
#ASSERT `the statement is deemed untrue` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is deemed untrue` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `the report or memorandum is deemed included in the statement in lieu of prospectus` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the report or memorandum is deemed included in the statement in lieu of prospectus` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the report or memorandum is deemed included in the statement in lieu of prospectus` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the report or memorandum is deemed included in the statement in lieu of prospectus` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4(8) and 4(9) -- affairs of a corporation`

#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `section 8A`
#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `section 8C`
#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `section 8D`
#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `section 216`
#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `Part 9`
#ASSERT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `section 402`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4(8) defines "affairs" for this provision` `some other provision`

#ASSERT `the category is expressly among the affairs of a corporation` `the audit, working papers or auditor's reports`
#ASSERT `the category is expressly among the affairs of a corporation` `ownership of shares, debentures or interests issued by the corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the category is expressly among the affairs of a corporation` `something not on the list`

-- "Includes": being off the list does not show a matter is outside.
#ASSERT NOT `being absent from the list shows the matter is not an affair of the corporation` `something not on the list`
